WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.480
Everyone is counting the days until the opening of the great New York World's Fair, an exposition

00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:15.000
symbolized by the Unisphere that dominates the grounds.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.360
While we may be counting the days, the workmen are counting the hours, for many buildings

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:20.840
are yet to be completed.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.880
However, fair officials are confident that everything will be in readiness when the gates

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:29.120
finally open to an expected 70 million visitors.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.160
Most craftsmen are working round the clock to complete the work on time, and the job

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:49.560
is tremendous when you figure that there will be 196 exhibitors rolling out those red carpets.

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:54.040
Fifty-eight nations are to be represented from the African nations to the Vatican, and

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:56.880
they will have on display many priceless treasures.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:02.080
The theme of the fair is peace through understanding, and its aim is the fostering of mutual and

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:07.040
lasting respect and the furtherance of common interests and world peace.

00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:09.040
Each nation will reveal a corner of itself.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:14.200
For a moment you can be in the Far East, and then a step away in Europe.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:20.400
The fair covers 646 acres and is on the same site as the 1939 World's Fair.

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:25.160
It will run for six months this year, close for the winter, and reopen the following spring

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:26.800
for six months more.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:29.240
When you come, prepare to spend some time.

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:36.720
There will be plenty to see, plenty.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:43.680
Meanwhile, doff your hat to the workmen who are striving to beat that deadline.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.840
What is now a sea of mud will be rolling lawns.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:50.800
What looks like a jumble of metal and wood will be a sleek pavilion.

00:01:50.800 --> 00:01:55.640
The New York World's Fair of 1964 promises something for everyone.

00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:00.000
They have bet a billion-dollar investment and five years of planning.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.880
See you at the fair.

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.200
For the first time in nearly 30 years, a child movie star is immortalized at Grauman's Chinese

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:13.160
Theater, a Hollywood landmark.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:17.320
The teenage star being honored is Haley Mills, daughter of John Mills, who has scored her

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:20.360
latest hit in the film version of The Chalk Garden.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:24.760
Now Haley joins the ranks of Hollywood greats who have left their hand and footprints in

00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:28.800
the sidewalk before the theater, a big honor for a little girl.
